**ZEISS in India**

ZEISS in India is headquartered in Bengaluru and present in the fields of Industrial Quality Solutions, Research Microscopy Solutions, Medical Technology, Vision Care and Sports & Cine Optics.

ZEISS India has 3 production facilities, R&D center, Global IT services and about 40 Sales & Service offices in almost all Tier I and Tier II cities in India. With 2200+ employees and continued investments over 25 years in India, ZEISS’ success story in India is continuing at a rapid pace.

Further information at ZEISS India .

**Purpose of this position / Position summary**

**Your Talent, our Vision – together we see beyond. Your start at ZEISS Vision Care** . As a leading manufacturer of ophthalmic lenses, we help people around the world achieve clearer vision – sustainably and with focus on the future.

Our products are as diverse as the career paths we offer, from tailored lenses to award-winning measurement systems.

Become part of our team and shape a future in which clear vision and professional success go hand in hand.

The Business Analyst for Quality Management will support the global implementation and adoption of Veeva QMS capabilities within VISION. The role bridges Quality Management business processes and IT solution delivery by translating requirements from Quality, Manufacturing, Laboratory, Regulatory and related business functions into clear functional specifications, user stories, test scenarios and implementation deliverables. While the primary focus is the Veeva QMS implementation, a solid SAP QM baseline is required to understand existing quality processes, master data, inspection flows, quality notifications, certificates and integration touchpoints with SAP, LIMS, document management systems and other enterprise platforms. The position supports harmonized, compliant and scalable quality process design in regulated environments.

**Primary duties and responsibilities**

* Act as Business Analyst for the Veeva QMS implementation, supporting requirements engineering, process design, configuration clarification, testing, validation, rollout and hypercare activities;
* Collaborate with Quality Management, Manufacturing, Laboratory, Regulatory, IT and local business stakeholders to understand business needs and translate them into functional specifications and user stories;
* Support process and requirement definition for core Veeva QMS areas such as deviations, CAPA, change control, complaints, audits, document control, training, quality events and management reporting;
* Use SAP QM knowledge as a baseline to understand existing quality processes and integration dependencies, including inspection processes, QM master data, inspection lots, results recording, usage decision, quality notifications, quality certificates and quality reporting;
* Support integration analysis between Veeva QMS, SAP QM, LIMS, document management systems and related enterprise platforms, including master data alignment, process handovers, interface requirements, error handling and end-to-end traceability;
* Contribute to harmonized Veeva QMS process design across global and local quality requirements, ensuring alignment with existing SAP QM-based operational quality processes where relevant;
* Support document management and training-related requirements within the Veeva QMS implementation, including controlled documents, specifications, approval workflows, version control, training relevance and audit-ready document traceability;
* Prepare and maintain business process documentation, functional specifications, interface specifications, test scripts, validation evidence, training material and support documentation;
* Coordinate and support system testing, integration testing, user acceptance testing, defect resolution, cut-over preparation, go-live support and hypercare activities;
* Work closely with SAP functional consultants, integration teams, external implementation partners, validation teams and business process owners to ensure fit-for-purpose and compliant solutions;
* Support compliance with applicable quality, regulatory, computerized system validation, data integrity, ISO 13485, GxP and internal governance requirements where applicable;
Drive continuous improvement by identifying process gaps, proposing harmonized Veeva QMS solutions and supporting adoption of standardized quality management processes across sites.  




**1. Education / Professional Certification**

University degree in Business Informatics, Computer Science, Engineering, Quality Management, Life Sciences, Business Administration, or an equivalent qualification.  



**2. Experience**

Minimum 5 years of relevant professional experience as a Business Analyst, Process Expert, Functional Consultant or similar role in quality management system implementation or quality process digitalization, preferably with exposure to Veeva QMS or comparable electronic QMS platforms. Solid SAP QM knowledge is required as a baseline, especially in inspection processes, QM master data, quality notifications, quality certificates, LIMS integration and quality-related enterprise system integration.  



**3. Knowledge / Skills / Other characteristics**

* Strong understanding of Quality Management processes and electronic QMS implementation topics, preferably including Veeva QMS capabilities such as deviations, CAPA, change control, complaints, audits, document control, training, quality events and management reporting;
* Solid SAP QM baseline knowledge, including inspection planning, inspection lot processing, results recording, usage decision, quality notifications, quality certificates, quality reporting and relevant QM master data objects;
